    ├── Used APIs  : dumps(record, sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':'))
    ├── Pitfalls   : ujson historically has inconsistent support for the `separators` argument across versions — verify compact separators still produce ',' 
    │   and ':' exactly, or output will not be byte-identical; ujson float/large-int formatting can differ slightly from stdlib json, risking non-determinism 
    │   in numeric serialization; simplejson is closest to full API compatibility but is a separate dependency to add/pin; Any change to separator or 
    │   key-ordering behavior breaks the stated 'byte-reproducible' audit log guarantee, so exact output must be verified with tests before switching
    └── The file's own docstring identifies `json` as a substitution target for a faster drop-in JSON encoder. `simplejson` is a near-exact drop-in for stdlib 
        `json`, supporting the same `sort_keys` and `separators` keyword arguments needed for deterministic, byte-reproducible output. `ujson` is also commonly
        used as a faster substitute and supports `sort_keys`, though its handling of custom `separators` is more limited/version-dependent than 
        `json`/`simplejson`.

