│    14 def _axiom_json_dumps_wrapper(record, sort_keys=True, separators=_SEPARATORS):                                                                        │
│    15     """Serialize ``record`` to a JSON string with the same guarantees stdlib                                                                          │
│    16     ``json.dumps(record, sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":"))`` gave us.                                                                            │
│    17                                                                                                                                                       │
│    18     stdlib ``json.dumps`` accepts a ``separators`` keyword and controls                                                                               │
│    19     numeric formatting via Python's ``float.__repr__``, producing a fixed,                                                                            │
│    20     compact, byte-reproducible string (no stray whitespace, deterministic                                                                             │
│    21     float text like ``1.0`` / ``1e+100``).                                                                                                            │
│    22                                                                                                                                                       │
│    23     ``ujson.dumps`` supports ``sort_keys`` but its handling of ``separators``                                                                         │
│    24     is inconsistent across versions (it may ignore the kwarg entirely), and                                                                           │
│    25     its numeric formatting for floats/large ints can diverge slightly from                                                                            │
│    26     stdlib json (different trailing zeros, exponent casing, etc.). Passing                                                                            │
│    27     ``separators`` straight through is therefore unreliable.                                                                                          │
│    28                                                                                                                                                       │
│    29     This wrapper calls ``ujson.dumps`` with only ``sort_keys`` (letting                                                                               │
│    30     ujson pick whatever separator style it wants), then walks the resulting                                                                           │
│    31     text -- skipping over string literals so we never touch user data --                                                                              │
│    32     and: (1) rewrites every structural ',' and ':' to use the requested                                                                               │
│    33     compact separators with no trailing whitespace, and (2) re-renders every                                                                          │
│    34     numeric literal that looks like a float (contains '.', 'e' or 'E')                                                                                │
│    35     through Python's own ``repr(float(...))`` so the digits match exactly                                                                             │
│    36     what stdlib ``json.dumps`` would have emitted. Integers are left as-is                                                                            │
│    37     since their textual form can't diverge. This keeps the audit log                                                                                  │
│    38     byte-reproducible regardless of the ujson version's quirks.                                                                                       │
